1
00:00:00,053 --> 00:00:02,760
There are over 8 billion people on Earth.

2
00:00:02,766 --> 00:00:04,722
But what if we're all related?

3
00:00:04,484 --> 00:00:06,202
Let's climb our friend's family tree.

4
00:00:06,112 --> 00:00:08,336
He has 2 parents, 4 grandparents,

5
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:10,067
and 8 great-grandparents.

6
00:00:10,075 --> 00:00:12,391
Every generation back, the number doubles!

7
00:00:12,281 --> 00:00:15,249
30 generations back, about 800 years ago,

8
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:16,302
his tree has over

9
00:00:16,302 --> 00:00:18,539
a billion ancestor slots. But back then,

10
00:00:18,539 --> 00:00:20,228
the whole world had only about

11
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:22,492
400 million people. So the same people

12
00:00:22,492 --> 00:00:24,484
fill many slots, again and again.

13
00:00:24,489 --> 00:00:26,085
And everyone's family trees

14
00:00:26,085 --> 00:00:28,043
start to overlap. One model suggests

15
00:00:28,043 --> 00:00:30,210
everyone alive today may share an ancestor

16
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:32,126
from just a few thousand years ago.

17
00:00:31,877 --> 00:00:33,918
Now let's rewind much further.

18
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:35,433
Your family tree includes

19
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:37,020
everyone you descend from.

20
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,368
But your DNA comes from only some of them.

21
00:00:39,278 --> 00:00:41,173
DNA passed from mother to child

22
00:00:41,173 --> 00:00:43,979
traces back to one woman in Africa,

23
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:47,058
roughly 150,000–200,000 years ago.

24
00:00:47,063 --> 00:00:49,796
Scientists call her Mitochondrial Eve.

25
00:00:49,706 --> 00:00:51,466
DNA passed from father to son

26
00:00:51,466 --> 00:00:53,005
traces men back to one man:

27
00:00:53,005 --> 00:00:56,062
Y-chromosomal Adam. They weren't a couple,

28
00:00:56,062 --> 00:00:57,298
and probably didn't even

29
00:00:57,298 --> 00:00:58,473
live at the same time.

30
00:00:58,386 --> 00:00:59,059
Scientists can trace

31
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,407
certain genetic lineages

32
00:01:00,407 --> 00:01:01,586
back to common ancestors.

33
00:01:01,586 --> 00:01:03,341
But these weren't the only people

34
00:01:03,341 --> 00:01:05,711
alive at the time. Their lines are simply

35
00:01:05,711 --> 00:01:07,458
the ones that never broke.

36
00:01:07,265 --> 00:01:09,525
Later, people moved out of Africa

37
00:01:09,525 --> 00:01:10,968
and spread across the globe,

38
00:01:10,972 --> 00:01:12,905
into Asia, Europe, Australia,

39
00:01:12,905 --> 00:01:15,222
and the Americas. Just think about it.

40
00:01:15,224 --> 00:01:18,288
Everyone watching this, in Japan, Brazil,

41
00:01:18,288 --> 00:01:21,844
or Turkey, is your distant relative.

42
00:01:21,608 --> 00:01:23,104
8 billion people. Billions of

43
00:01:23,104 --> 00:01:24,706
family stories. And a past that's

44
00:01:24,706 --> 00:01:26,795
far more connected than you think.

